30, 2025, the Company terminated the lease in accordance with a lease amendment entered into with the landlord. Accordingly, the Company accelerated the amortization of the right-of-use asset to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-188" decimals="-5" name="us-gaap:OperatingLeaseRightOfUseAsset" format="ixt:fixed-zero" scale="0" id="f-658">zero</ix:nonFraction> and adjusted the remaining lease obligation to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-188" decimals="-5" name="us-gaap:OperatingLeaseLiability" format="ixt:fixed-zero" scale="0" id="f-659">zero</ix:nonFraction> as of December 31, 2025. </span></div><div><span><br/></span></div><div><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">On April 29, 2026, the Company entered into a lease agreement for approximately <ix:nonFraction unitRef="sqft" contextRef="c-189" decimals="0" name="xfor:OfficeSpaceUnderLeaseAgreement" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="0" id="f-660">11,000</ix:nonFraction> square feet of office space in a building located in Watertown, Massachusetts (the &#8220;Watertown Lease&#8221;). The office space will replace the Company&#8217;s current headquarters located in Boston, Massachusetts. The Company intends to move into the premises in late 2026 or early 2027 upon the completion of construction, which is anticipated to commence in September 2026. Monthly rent payments under the lease will commence three months following the Company obtaining access to the space. Base rental payments will be approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-189" decimals="-5" name="us-gaap:LeaseAndRentalExpense" scale="6" id="f-661">0.3</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million annually, plus certain operating expenses. The term of the lease will continue for <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="c-190" name="us-gaap:LesseeOperatingLeaseTermOfContract" format="ixt-sec:durmonth" id="f-662">36</ix:nonNumeric> months following the commencement of rent payments, unless earlier terminated in accordance with the terms of the lease. The Company has the right to sublease the premises, subject to landlord consent. The Company also has the right to renew the lease for an additional <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="c-190" name="us-gaap:LesseeOperatingLeaseRenewalTerm" format="ixt-sec:duryear" id="f-663">3</ix:nonNumeric> years at the then prevailing effective market rental rate. The Company was required to provide the landlord with a $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-190" decimals="-5" name="us-gaap:SecurityDeposit" scale="6" id="f-664">0.1</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million letter of credit, which is classified as restricted cash.</span></div><div style="margin-top:6pt"><span><br/></span></div><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="c-1" name="us-gaap:LeaseCostTableTextBlock" id="f-665" escape="true"><div style="margin-top:6pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The components of lease expense for the three and six months ended June 30, 2026 and 2025 were as follows:</span></div><div style="margin-top:6pt"><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:42.905%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:12.057%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.530%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:12.057%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.700%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:12.057%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.530%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:12.064%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td colspan="3" style="display:none"/><td colspan="3" style="display:none"/><td colspan="3" style="display:none"/><td colspan="3" style="display:none"/